  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The correct order of hydration enthalpies is</p><p>(A)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math><br />(B)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Rb</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math><br />(C)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math><br />(D)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cs</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math><br />(E)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "krPhj",
      "text": "C &gt; A &gt; E &gt; B &gt; D",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wRDDD",
      "text": "E &gt; C &gt; A &gt; B &gt; D",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0eQnS",
      "text": "C &gt; E &gt; A &gt; D &gt; B",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IEy0d",
      "text": "C &gt; E &gt; A &gt; B &gt; D",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The hydration enthalpy of alkali metal ions decreases with an increase in ionic sizes.</p><p>So, the order is:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Li</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Rb</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Cs</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math></p><p>Like alkali metal ions, the hydration enthalpies of alkaline earth metal ions decrease with an increase in ionic size down the group.</p><p>So, the order is:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Be</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Sr</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Ba</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;</p><p>The hydration enthalpies of alkaline earth metal ions are larger than those of alkali metal ions.&nbsp;</p><p>So, the correct order is:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Rb</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Cs</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
